      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-10-27",
      "edition": "Tuesday 27 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad availability",
          "heading": "Italy are missing 12 players for next month's Nations Championship",
          "body": "Italy are missing 12 players for next month's Nations Championship, a count that puts real pressure on Gonzalo Quesada's preparations before the autumn begins. The absences sit alongside the Menoncello setback: the Toulouse centre is set to miss the autumn Tests with a left-shoulder sprain, and Italy face South Africa, Argentina and Fiji before travelling to London for the Nations Championship Finals Weekend. After three summer defeats to Japan, New Zealand and Australia, depth is the question Quesada now has to answer."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji beat Japan 34-28 in the centenary Test",
          "body": "Shaun Edwards signs as Argentina defence coach. Ardie Savea left out of New Zealand's Nations Championship squad. Ireland wings Tommy and Jimmy O'Brien forced off in URC interpro."
        }
      ]
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-10-27",
      "edition": "Tuesday 27 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad selection",
          "heading": "Townsend warns fringe men that breaking into Scotland's squad won't be easy",
          "body": "Townsend has warned fringe players that breaking into his Scotland squad won't be easy, and the 37-man group for November's block is a tough one to crack. Jack Dempsey keeps his place despite leaving Glasgow for Japan, while Huw Jones returns after missing the July tour through injury. Scotland host New Zealand at Murrayfield before Australia and Japan, with Ollie Leatherbarrow the only uncapped name in the group."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji beat Japan 34-28 in the centenary Test",
          "body": "Shaun Edwards signs as Argentina defence coach. Ardie Savea left out of New Zealand's Nations Championship squad. Ireland wings Tommy and Jimmy O'Brien forced off in URC interpro."
        }
      ]
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-10-27",
      "edition": "Tuesday 27 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad recall",
          "heading": "Dillon Lewis rejoins Wales squad for November Tests after two-year gap",
          "body": "Dragons tight-head Dillon Lewis has joined Steve Tandy's squad for the four November Tests, after two years away. The 30-year-old made four summer starts, against the Barbarians, Fiji, Argentina and South Africa, and admits he came back with doubts about whether he was still good enough. Tomas Francis being rested and Archie Griffin's toe surgery opened the door, but both are back now, so Lewis faces a battle for the tight-head berth. \"I got thrown straight in with four starts, so hopefully they liked what they saw.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji beat Japan 34-28 in the centenary Test",
          "body": "Shaun Edwards signs as Argentina defence coach. Ardie Savea left out of New Zealand's Nations Championship squad. Ireland wings Tommy and Jimmy O'Brien forced off in URC interpro."
